ly of foreign origin;","strongs_def":"Nimrod, a son of Cush","kjv_def":"Nimrod.","n":4,"o":"GEN10:8 GEN10:9 1CH1:10 MIC5:6"},"H5249":{"lemma":"נִמְרִים","xlit":"Nimrîym","pron":"nim-reem'","derivation":"plural of a masculine corresponding to H5247 (נִמְרָה); clear waters;","strongs_def":"Nimrim, a place East of the Jordan","kjv_def":"Nimrim. Compare H1039 (בֵּית נִמְרָה).","n":2,"o":"ISA15:6 JER48:34"},"H5250":{"lemma":"נִמְשִׁי","xlit":"Nimshîy","pron":"nim-shee'","derivation":"probably from H4871 (מָשָׁה); extricated;","strongs_def":"Nimshi, the (grand-) father of Jehu","kjv_def":"Nimshi.","n":5,"o":"1KI19:16 2KI9:2 2KI9:14 2KI9:20 2CH22:7"},"H5251":{"lemma":"נֵס","xlit":"nêç","pron":"nace","derivation":"from H5264 (נָסַס);","strongs_def":"a flag; also a sail; by implication, a flagstaff; generally a signal; figuratively, a token","kjv_def":"banner, pole, sail, (en-) sign, standard.","n":20,"o":"NUM21:8 NUM21:9 NUM26:10 PSA60:4 ISA5:26 ISA11:10 ISA11:12 ISA13:2 ISA18:3 ISA30:17 ISA31:9 ISA33:23 ISA49:22 ISA62:10 JER4:6 JER4:21 JER50:2 JER51:12 JER51:27 EZK27:7"},"H5252":{"lemma":"נְסִבָּה","xlit":"nᵉçibbâh","pron":"nes-ib-baw'","derivation":"feminine participle passive of H5437 (סָבַב);","strongs_def":"properly, an environment, i.e. circumstance or turn of affairs","kjv_def":"cause.","n":1,"o":"2CH10:15"},"H5253":{"lemma":"נָסַג","xlit":"nâçag","pron":"naw-sag'","derivation":"a primitive root;","strongs_def":"to retreat","kjv_def":"departing away, remove, take (hold), turn away.","n":9,"o":"DEU19:14 DEU27:17 PRO22:28 PRO23:10 ISA59:13 ISA59:14 HOS5:10 MIC2:6 MIC6:14"},"H5254":{"lemma":"נָסָה","xlit":"nâçâh","pron":"naw-saw'","derivation":"a primitive root;","strongs_def":"to test; by implication, to attempt","kjv_def":"adventure, assay, prove, tempt, try.","n":34,"o":"GEN22:1 EXO15:25 EXO16:4 EXO17:2 EXO17:7 EXO20:20 NUM14:22 DEU4:34 DEU6:16 DEU8:2 DEU8:16 DEU13:3 DEU28:56 DEU33:8 JDG2:22 JDG3:1 JDG3:4 JDG6:39 1SA17:39 1KI10:1 2CH9:1 2CH32:31 JOB4:2 PSA26:2 PSA78: